WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
What can an in-depth interview reveal that a group may miss?

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:10.000
It creates space to follow one person’s experience, reasoning and context.

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:12.400
Begin with a specific example.

00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:18.160
Ask what happened, what the person understood, and what they did next.

00:00:18.160 --> 00:00:22.000
Use open questions instead of suggesting the answer.

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:27.143
A discussion guide keeps the research focused, while follow-up questions explore details

00:00:27.143 --> 00:00:29.714
the team may not have anticipated.

00:00:29.714 --> 00:00:34.000
It is a guide, not a script for the participant.

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:38.000
Interviews can suit complex, specialized or personal topics.

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:44.000
They still need clear consent and data-handling arrangements, and their findings are

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:46.000
not a population percentage.

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:51.778
If a larger study already exists, specify whether the work covers interviewing,

00:00:51.778 --> 00:00:54.185
analysis, or the whole study.

00:00:54.185 --> 00:00:59.000
Clear responsibilities help the research team use the contribution correctly.

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:05.940
PRC Impact provides qualitative study and interview support.

00:01:05.940 --> 00:01:14.616
Talk through your research question at prcimpact.com, or call 334-429-6994.
